@startuml "Not Flyweight - Object Pool - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title NOT Flyweight — an object pool, and why it is not


class ConnectionPool {
  - available : BlockingQueue
  + borrow(timeoutMs) : PooledConnection
  + release(conn)
}

class PooledConnection {
  - id : int
  - inUse : boolean
  + markInUse()
  + markFree()
  + query(sql)
}

ConnectionPool o-- PooledConnection

note right of ConnectionPool
  <b>borrow / release.</b> A flyweight
  factory has no release, because
  there is nothing to give back.
end note

note bottom of PooledConnection
  <b>Mutable, and exclusive.</b> One holder
  at a time; two would be the bug.

  A flyweight is held by everybody
  at once, which is safe only because
  it is immutable.

  Pool saves <b>time</b>.
  Flyweight saves <b>memory</b>.
end note

@enduml
